{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/785889-question-on-obfuscate-vampire-2nd-edition","id":785889,"title":"Question on Obfuscate. (vampire 2nd edition)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-14T04:28:16-08:00","id":785889,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Question on Obfuscate. (vampire 2nd edition)","content":"&quot;Used with Cloak of Night, Touch of Shadow can now affect<br /> other people. The normal rules for piercing Touch of Shadow<br /> apply. Some vampires steal their victims from the world, feeding<br /> upon them as the mass of humanity walks on by.&quot;<br /> <br /> This means that i have to spend 2 vitae to activate obfuscate 2 and 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10250-gabry1989","name":"gabry1989","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T05:01:21-08:00","id":785900,"title":"","content":"Its a bit more complicated than that. You don't really &quot;activate&quot; Obfuscate 3 at all. Instead, Obfuscate 3 only modifies 1 and 2, and only when you want them to. Normally, Face in the Crowd just makes you unremarkable, and people not pay attention to you; they'll still see you out of the corner of their eye, but don't consider you important. With Cloak of Night, the vampire can choose to spend a point of vitae and vanish from sight entirely instead of using the normal effect. People staring directly at the vampire will see them fade away as the power is activated. <br /> <br /> With Touch of Shadows, you can choose to either stay with the normal effect, and make an object or person unremarkable for the cost of 1 vitae, or you can make them vanish from sight with the cost of 2 vitae.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T05:18:27-08:00","id":785907,"title":"","content":"completely clear:<br /> vanish entirely for 1 vitae, make someone vanish with 2 vitae or make a person unremarkable (instead of an object like for obfuscate 2) with 1 vitae. Thanks a lot<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10250-gabry1989","name":"gabry1989","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T09:49:59-08:00","id":786044,"title":"","content":"Should the vanished one stay close to the obfuscate owner or can she take some distance? And if yes, how far could she go to stay invisible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}